#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:179
msgid "IMAP4 Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:181
msgid ""
"All IMAP4rev1 commands are represented by methods of the same name, either "
"uppercase or lowercase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:184
msgid ""
"All arguments to commands are converted to strings, except for "
"``AUTHENTICATE``, and the last argument to ``APPEND`` which is passed as an "
"IMAP4 literal.  If necessary (the string contains IMAP4 protocol-sensitive "
"characters and isn't enclosed with either parentheses or double quotes) each "
"string is quoted. However, the *password* argument to the ``LOGIN`` command "
"is always quoted. If you want to avoid having an argument string quoted (eg: "
"the *flags* argument to ``STORE``) then enclose the string in parentheses "
"(eg: ``r'(\\Deleted)'``). Or you can quote the string yourself; an argument "
"that is already enclosed in double quotes is left unchanged. In general, "
"however, it is better to pass arguments unquoted and let the module quote "
"them as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:196
msgid ""
"Mailbox names are encoded as modified UTF-7 (:rfc:`3501`, section 5.1.3), so "
"a mailbox name containing non-ASCII characters can be passed as an ordinary :"
"class:`str`. A :class:`str` that is already valid modified UTF-7 is left "
"unchanged, so that a name obtained from :meth:`~IMAP4.list` (raw ``bytes`` "
"decoded to text) round-trips; pass :class:`bytes` to send the exact bytes "
"with no encoding. When ``UTF8=ACCEPT`` is enabled (see :meth:`~IMAP4."
"enable`), mailbox names are sent as UTF-8 instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:206
msgid "Non-ASCII mailbox names are automatically encoded as modified UTF-7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:209
msgid ""
"Most commands return a tuple: ``(type, [data, ...])`` where *type* is "
"usually ``'OK'`` or ``'NO'``, and *data* is either the text from the command "
"response, or mandated results from the command. Each *data* is either a "
"``bytes``, or a tuple. If a tuple, then the first part is the header of the "
"response, and the second part contains the data (ie: 'literal' value)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:215
msgid ""
"The *message_set* options to the commands below can be a string specifying "
"one or more messages to be acted upon. It may be a simple message number "
"(``'1'``), a range of message numbers (``'2:4'``), or a group of non-"
"contiguous ranges separated by commas (``'1:3,6:9'``). A range can contain "
"an asterisk to indicate an infinite upper bound (``'3:*'``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:223
msgid ""
"Alternatively it can be specified using integers and :class:`range` objects. "
"It may be a single message number or a sequence. The sequence items may be "
"integers, ``(start, stop)`` tuples (where ``None`` or ``'*'`` stands for the "
"last message), or :class:`range` objects. For example, ``[1, (3, 5), 8]`` "
"and ``[range(1, 6), 8]`` are both equivalent to ``'1,3:5,8'``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:231
msgid "Added support for the structured *message_set*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:234
msgid ""
"Command arguments that are parenthesized lists of atoms --- such as the "
"*flag_list* argument of :meth:`~IMAP4.store` and the *flags* argument of :"
"meth:`~IMAP4.append`, the *names* argument of :meth:`~IMAP4.status`, the "
"*sort_criteria* argument of :meth:`~IMAP4.sort`, or the *message_parts* "
"argument of :meth:`~IMAP4.fetch` --- can be passed as a sequence of strings "
"instead of a single preformatted string. For example, ``[r'\\Seen', "
"r'\\Answered']`` is equivalent to ``(\\Seen \\Answered)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:244
msgid "Added support for passing these arguments as a sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:249
msgid ""
"The value-bearing arguments of the search and fetch commands can be quoted "
"by hand, but this is error prone. Instead, they may contain ``?`` "
"placeholders that are substituted, and quoted as required, from a *params* "
"keyword argument, in the manner of :mod:`sqlite3` parameter substitution::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:261
msgid "The placeholders are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:263
msgid ""
"``?`` --- an ``astring``: a string (which will be quoted if necessary), an "
"integer, or a list of integers and/or strings (which will be sent as a "
"parenthesized list);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:266
msgid "``?f`` --- a flag or a list of flags, sent verbatim without quoting;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:267
msgid "``?s`` --- a *message_set* in the structured form described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:269
msgid "``??`` stands for a literal ``?``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/imaplib.rst:271
msgid ""
"Substitution is only performed when *params* is given; if no *params* are "
"given, an argument containing a literal ``?`` is unchanged. The *params* "
"keyword is accepted by :meth:`~IMAP4.search`, :meth:`~IMAP4.fetch`, :meth:"
"`~IMAP4.sort`, :meth:`~IMAP4.thread` and :meth:`~IMAP4.uid`."
msgstr ""

